      - It does not currently accept the required author dict and does not currently implement priority-ordered alternate-names/surname matching.
    - `find_entity(author)` is currently around line 161.
      - Verified: it reads `author['name']`, calls `find_author(name)`, optionally also tries `find_author(flip_name(name))` when `', '` is in the name, then filters by birth/death-date presence and `author_dates_match`.
      - It currently relies on exact/case-sensitive name lookup via `find_author`, not ILIKE-style matching.
      - It does not currently attempt `alternate_names` or surname-specific matching.
    - `pick_from_matches` exists around line 114 and is used when multiple matches remain.
    - Existing behavior was observed via ad hoc scripts:
