Requirements list:
1. `find_entity(author: dict)` attempts resolution in priority order: name+dates, alternate_names+dates, surname+dates.
2. When both birth_date and death_date present in input, they must be used to disambiguate, exact year match for both takes precedence.
3. When either date absent, fall back to case-insensitive name matching alone; existing author record returned if one exists under that name.
4. Case-insensitive matching; different casings resolve to same record.
5. Wildcards: `"John*"` returns first candidate by numeric key ordering; if no match, a new author candidate is returned preserving input name including `*`.
6. Match via alternate_names requires both birth_date and death_date present in input and exactly matching candidate values when dates are available.
7. Match via surname requires both dates present and exactly matching; surname path must not resolve if either date missing or mismatched.
8. If no valid match, return a new author candidate dict preserving name, birth_date, death_date unchanged.
9. Year comparison considers only the year component; any year difference invalidates match.
10. `find_author(author: dict)` accepts the author import dict and returns a list of candidate author records consistent with matching rules; `find_entity(author: dict)` delegates to `find_author` and returns existing record or None.

